note.text:
Matter exists as solid, liquid or gas.
• Solid: fixed shape and volume. Liquid: fixed volume, takes the shape of its container. Gas: fills its container, can be compressed.
Changes of state are physical changes:
• melting (solid → liquid) at the melting point; ice melts at 0 °C;
• freezing (liquid → solid);
• evaporation and boiling (liquid → gas); water boils at 100 °C;
• condensation (gas → liquid);
• sublimation (solid → gas directly), for example iodine and ammonium chloride.
A pure substance melts and boils at fixed temperatures; an impure one melts and boils over a range.
